From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rtworkq: Don't hold queues_section while shutting down the
 system queues.

shutdown_system_queues() held queues_section across shutdown_queue(),
which waits for the running pool callbacks. A callback that unlocks a
user queue takes queues_section too, so MFShutdown() deadlocked with it:

  thread A: MFShutdown -> RtwqShutdown -> shutdown_system_queues
            (holds queues_section, waits for the callback)
  thread B: source reader callback -> RtwqUnlockWorkQueue
            (waits for queues_section)

unlock_user_queue() already shuts its queue down outside the lock.

Shut the standard queue down first, without the lock. grab_queue() then
fails, and it now rechecks that under the lock, so no new system queue
is created behind us; taking the lock once waits for one still being
created. Then shut the other system queues down, also without the lock.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/899
---
--- a/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
+++ b/dlls/rtworkq/queue.c
@@ -665,6 +665,18 @@
         struct queue_desc desc;
 
         EnterCriticalSection(&queues_section);
+        /* Don't create a system queue after shutdown_system_queues() went past it. */
+        if (!system_queues[SYS_QUEUE_STANDARD].pool)
+        {
+            LeaveCriticalSection(&queues_section);
+            return RTWQ_E_SHUTDOWN;
+        }
+        if (queue->pool)
+        {
+            LeaveCriticalSection(&queues_section);
+            *ret = queue;
+            return S_OK;
+        }
         switch (queue_id)
         {
             case RTWQ_CALLBACK_QUEUE_IO:
@@ -1310,17 +1322,26 @@
     unsigned int i;
     HRESULT hr;
 
+    /* Shutting down a pool queue waits for its running callbacks, which may
+     * need queues_section themselves, e.g. to unlock a user queue. Don't hold
+     * it while waiting.
+     *
+     * Once the standard queue is shut down, grab_queue() fails and creates no
+     * more system queues. Taking the lock waits for one that is still being
+     * created, so that it is shut down below. */
+    shutdown_queue(&system_queues[SYS_QUEUE_STANDARD]);
+
     EnterCriticalSection(&queues_section);
+    LeaveCriticalSection(&queues_section);
 
     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(system_queues); ++i)
     {
+        if (i == SYS_QUEUE_STANDARD) continue;
         shutdown_queue(&system_queues[i]);
     }
 
     if (FAILED(hr = CoDecrementMTAUsage(mta_cookie)))
         WARN("Failed to uninitialize MTA, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
-
-    LeaveCriticalSection(&queues_section);
 }
 
 HRESULT WINAPI RtwqShutdown(void)
